{
  "format": "wildlands-process",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "revision": 0,
  "id": "order-fulfilment-line",
  "name": "Order fulfilment line",
  "description": "Synthetic steady random demand on an order fulfilment line. Orders arrive as an open stream with a random gap (exponential, mean 4 minutes, at most 12) and keep arriving for as long as the run lasts, so the line is meant to run unlimited. Each order draws a priority (20% express, 80% standard) and a 12% chance of a known defect. Orders pass software checks, parallel picking robots and shipping documents, three parallel packing lanes, a human spot-check by three inspectors with a bounded repack loop, a label machine and a customer notification. Picking (triangular 4/6/10), packing (uniform 7 to 11) and the spot-check (uniform 4 to 8) take random whole minutes around their mean duration. The Passed? decision sends a known defect to repack, and a further 6% chance route sends a parcel to repack as damaged in transit; both use the same repack step. Every random value derives from the definition seed 20260607 and the case, step and visit, so the same seed always gives the same run and another seed (process run --seed N) gives another one. Capacities are tuned so the packing lanes run at roughly three quarters of capacity; a brief system-full refusal is possible but not expected. All values are synthetic illustrative assumptions, not a measured warehouse or a forecast.",
  "start": "order-received",
